WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.467
-Welcome back! We have such
a great show for you tonight.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.868
And you know what?
Before we go, I'm just --

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.634
I'm a little hungry.
If you don't mind,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.868
I just want to grab something
from the "Tonight Show" freezer

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.367
real quick.
It'll take a second.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.267
It just -- I'm so sorry
about this. I'm sorry.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.267
Thank you guys so much.
I appreciate it.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:21.667
♪♪

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:25.100
-♪ Freezer Secrets ♪

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.434
♪♪

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:30.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh! No, no!

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.667
No, no, no! I'm --
Help, help! I'm --

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:37.033
Help, I'm stuck in the freezer!
I'm stuck in the freezer.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.767
Oh, gosh, I --

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.667
-It's no use.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.067
-Fred Armisen?
What are you doing in here?

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.634
-I thought this was
the dressing room.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.501
and I just left the window open.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.501
-This is awful.
I knew it was a mistake

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.367
buying a soundproof freezer.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.634
I knew -- I knew it.
We're doomed.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:03.701
-Well, since this is the end,
I guess I have a few secrets

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:05.901
I need to get off my chest.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.734
-Same.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.334
-All right.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.901
You know that new Harry Styles
song, "Watermelon Sugar?"

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.100
-Of course. Yeah, I listen
to it every day. It's new.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.701
-Well, it took me...
[ Laughs ]

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.400
Brand new. It took me
an embarrassing amount of time

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.701
to realize that the song
is actually a double entendre.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.434
-Right, right, right. And --

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:29.000
-It's about diabetes.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.167
♪♪

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.934
-One time I saw Yoplait yogurt

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:39.834
in the fridge with my coworker
Bethany's name on it.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.000
I took it anyway and ate it.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.801
-Oh, yeah. I did something
similar once.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.901
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.901
I caused
the 2008 financial crisis.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.434
-That's not similar at all.
I mean, that --

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.133
And how did you do that?

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.934
-I don't know.
I had a day off and I was bored.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:04.534
-In the '90, I had a bitter feud
with the Taco Bell Chihuahua.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:08.067
-I get it, but why?

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.133
-We auditioned
for the same part.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.501
We are the final two
in the running

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.801
to be Taco Bell's
new spokeschihuahua.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:18.300
He beat me out because
I was six feet tall and a human.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.501
-Have you talked to him since?
-Nah, nah, nah.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:24.133
Once he had that gordita money,
he became a real monster.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.367
-I have one.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.968
I used to work
as a part-time exorcist,

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.868
but I got fired
because I was too polite

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.167
with the demonic entities.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.901
I'd say the power of Christ

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.901
would prefer
you get out of here.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.868
The power of Christ
is going to count to three.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:41.534
One, two, two and a half...

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.701
-Okay, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.601
I've lied about my age,
my whole career.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.367
I'm actually 96.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.334
You know those prosthetics
that Johnny Knoxville wears

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.567
in "Bad Grandpa?"
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.834
Amazing prosthetics.
-Yeah, well,

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.067
he let me borrow them,

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:57.834
and I wear them inside out
to make me look younger.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:00.400
-I have a secret family.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.267
-Fred, you're not married.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.033
I think you need to be married
with kids in order

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.000
to have a second family
that's a secret.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
-Oh, okay. In that case,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.467
I just have a regular family
that I don't like.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.200
[ Laughs ]

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.067
♪♪

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:18.534
-You know how I have that side
job as a valet in Vatican City?

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.234
-Of course, everyone knows
that about you.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:23.501
-Yeah, but, well, sometimes --
sometimes at night, I --

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.067
I take the Popemobile.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.267
♪♪

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.434
Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:36.501
♪♪

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:40.334
Sometimes -- Sometimes at night.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:43.934
I... [ Laughs ]

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:47.534
I-I take the Popemobile out --
[ Laughs ]

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.167
I take the Popemobile out
for a joyride.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.200
-No, that's --

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.601
That's fine. Live a little.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:53.934
-Yeah. Yeah. Well, well, well.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.467
The Pope has
a limited edition

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.834
"Minions: The Rise of Gru"
Big Gulp cup

00:03:57.834 --> 00:04:00.501
and I drank out of it.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.667
-I never graduated
from high school.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.367
-Well, that's nothing
to be ashamed of.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:07.434
-Because I accidentally
killed my principal.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.934
-W-What?
-As he was handing me

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:12.200
my diploma, I threw my cap up
in the air too early,

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.834
and one of those sharp points
hit him right this angle,

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:17.067
and it sliced him
completely in half.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.601
-Oh, my God.
How is that possible?

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:22.234
-My hat was made of metal.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.200
It was my final project
for shop class.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.834
I got a "B."

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.968
-You know, M&amp;M's old slogan,

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.400
"Melts in your mouth,
not in your hands?"

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.067
-Yeah?
-I have a rare medical condition

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:36.334
where M&amp;Ms melt in my hands
and not in my mouth.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.934
-I don't actually need
to wear glasses.

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:42.300
I only wear them
so people think I'm cool.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.901
-I'm in the same boat.
I actually don't have eyeballs.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.701
I stole these from
a Build-A-Bear workshop.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:59.000
-Wow. I guess I never noticed.
You have such beady, dead eyes.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.501
-Thank you.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:04.767
I mean, I shouldn't thank you.
I should thank Build-A-Bear.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.767
-I can't keep this
to myself anymore.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.300
I'm having a non-sexual,
non-romantic affair

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.000
with my dentist, Dr. Jimenez.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.033
He just cleans my teeth,

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.667
I exchange insurance info
with the front desk person,

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:19.267
and then I leave.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.834
-I don't think that's an affair.
-Oh, yeah?

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:25.234
Then how do you explain
the steamy voicemail he left me?

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.701
-Hi, Fred.
This is Amanda calling

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.033
from Dr. Jimenez's office.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.300
You have a tooth
cleaning scheduled

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.934
for June 20th at 9 a.m..

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:36.167
-Wow, he is in love with you,

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:38.133
-Fred? Jimmy?

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:39.200
-What? Higgins!

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.601
We're saved!

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.334
-What are you guys doing
in the men's room?

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.434
-This isn't the men's room.
It's a freezer.

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:48.767
-Oh, nobody told me that.
Don't look in that corner.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:51.300
[ Both shouting indistinctly ]

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.601
-Those aren't Baby Ruth bars.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.567
-This has been
Freezer Secrets.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:06:00.133
Stick around for more
"Tonight Show" after the break.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:03.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.133
♪♪

